From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pypi/build.sh: match the interpreter dir exactly

pypi/build.sh resolves each requested interpreter with
`ls /opt/python/${py}-*/bin/python`, which assumed exactly one `/opt/python`
entry per short tag (`cp312-cp312`). The riscv64 manylinux image also ships a
free-threaded build alongside the regular one under a shared prefix
(`cp314-cp314` and `cp314-cp314t`), so for `py=cp314` the glob matches both
directories and `ls` returns two lines, which `python=$(...)` collapses into
one broken multi-line value and aborts the build.

Build the exact path instead of globbing: `/opt/python/${py}-${py}/bin/python`
resolves unambiguously for every tag this workflow passes (cp312, cp313,
cp314), matching how the project's own later CI runs already invoke it in
practice (observed in the pyboolector-3.2.4.19342042739 sdist on PyPI, which
carries this same fix though it was never committed to this git repository).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 image splits cp314/cp314t under one shared /opt/python prefix]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/pypi/build.sh b/pypi/build.sh
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/pypi/build.sh
+++ b/pypi/build.sh
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
 cd pyboolector

 for py in $PYTHON_VERSIONS; do
-  python=$(ls /opt/python/${py}-*/bin/python)
+  python=/opt/python/${py}-${py}/bin/python
   echo "Python: ${python}"
   ${python} -m pip install cython wheel
   cd ${BUILD_DIR}/pyboolector
